implementationPlan.description:
Production, VS Code. File: moe-vscode/src/services/MoeDaemonClient.ts. Change only pathForms (about line 379) and add one new private helper beside it.

When does pathForms push a second form, missingRealPath(forms[0])? When all three hold:
- the native realpath of p fails with ENOENT;
- the host is Windows: process.platform === 'win32', the host default every predicate here uses, never the test-only windows parameter;
- the resolved spelling forms[0] is not isWindowsAlias, so no UNC or device spelling is walked or looked up again.

missingRealPath(resolved) walks dir = resolved upward. At each level whose realpath came back ENOENT:
1. Call lstatSync(dir). If it succeeds, the entry exists but does not resolve (a dangling junction or symlink): throw.
2. On lstat ENOENT, prepend path.basename(dir) to the tail and set dir = path.dirname(dir). If dirname returns dir unchanged (a drive root, e.g. a removed drive), throw: there is no existing ancestor.
3. Try fs.realpathSync.native(dir). On success, return path.join(real, ...tail). On ENOENT, continue. Rethrow any other code.

Error handling: every throw lands in isOutsideProject's existing catch, so the answer is false and the entry is dropped (fail closed).

The pushed form goes through the existing checks unchanged:
- isWindowsAlias refuses a UNC real path, such as a mapped drive's;
- the folded isWithin compares it against both project forms.

Keep unchanged:
- the ENOENT-only tolerance and its comment;
- every export and signature;
- POSIX: no walk off win32;
- the imports: add none, because seven vm harnesses use closed require maps.
Add one comment line on the why: a folder created there later is searched where its nearest existing ancestor really is (a link, 8.3 name, subst or mapped drive).

Re-run the step-1 native command: GREEN. Then run `cd moe-vscode && npm test` under WSL Linux: every existing row passes and the new row is skipped.

implementationPlan.note:
MoeDaemonClient.ts +22/-0, no imports added. When realpath returns ENOENT, pathForms now pushes missingRealPath(forms[0]), but only on process.platform === 'win32' and only when the resolved spelling is not isWindowsAlias. The ENOENT-only tolerance and its comment are unchanged.

missingRealPath walks up from the resolved spelling:
- lstat succeeds: throws 'an existing path does not resolve' (a dangling link);
- lstat fails with anything but ENOENT: rethrows;
- dirname reaches its fixed point: throws 'no existing ancestor';
- otherwise it tries realpath.native on the parent: a hit returns real + tail, ENOENT goes up one level, any other error is rethrown.
Every throw lands in isOutsideProject's catch, so the answer is false.

GREEN, native:
- the step-1 command exits 0, 1/1 pass, with no 8.3 or subst diagnostic, so every entry ran;
- protected-daemon-spawn + daemon-identity: 81 tests, 80 pass, 1 existing skip, 0 fail.
WSL Linux `cd moe-vscode && npm test`: 348 tests, 344 pass, 4 skipped (the new row plus 3 existing), 0 fail.
`npx eslint src/services/MoeDaemonClient.ts` exits 0. git diff --check is clean. subst lists nothing.
